      "startdescription": "The doctor is wiping his knife. The girl walks over and takes a careful look. The doctor says: 'Are you afraid of blood?' The girl says: 'No. Can you... teach me something?' The doctor stops his hands. When he looks at her, it is not as a patient, nor really as a soldier. More like looking at one of his own kind. Of course, I assure you Konstantin is human. Later, the two often exchange some bloody knowledge and knowledge on how not to make people bloody.",
